{"case_id":"T8027","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","state","configuration"],"commit_induced":"NO","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":93,"affected_functions":["LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput (fuzz/fuzz_implementations.cpp)","LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput (fuzz/fuzz_minifyimpl.cpp)","LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput (fuzz/fuzz_utf8.cpp)","simdjson::implementation::supported_by_runtime_system","main (tools/minify.cpp)"],"reason":"S1 exposes a runtime-support protocol that H0 does not observe: all three harnesses invoke every entry in simdjson::available_implementations without checking supported_by_runtime_system(), and fuzz_implementations.cpp also assigns each entry to simdjson::active_implementation. This can make harness execution depend on host CPU state. However, the gap was already present in S0: H0 already iterated all implementations while S0 already exposed required_instruction_sets() and detect_best_supported(), and the commit does not change parse(), minify(), validate_utf8(), backend availability, or H0's control of byte input. The commit merely adds a public convenience query and uses it for validation in tools/minify.cpp, so it does not introduce or materially aggravate the harness gap.","evidence":["implementation::supported_by_runtime_system() only compares required_instruction_sets() with detect_supported_architectures(); it introduces no fuzz-controlled input.","fuzz/fuzz_implementations.cpp iterates simdjson::available_implementations, sets simdjson::active_implementation=e.impl, and calls e.parser.parse(Data,Size) without a runtime-support check.","fuzz/fuzz_minifyimpl.cpp calls impl->minify(Data,Size,...) for every simdjson::available_implementations entry without a runtime-support check.","fuzz/fuzz_utf8.cpp calls impl->validate_utf8((const char*)Data,Size) for every simdjson::available_implementations entry without a runtime-support check.","S0 already declared required_instruction_sets() and available_implementation_list::detect_best_supported(), showing that runtime implementation suitability existed before this commit.","The production diff makes no changes to parser parsing, implementation::minify(), or implementation::validate_utf8(); H0 retains the same input reachability for those operations."],"recommended_action":"Do not attribute harness maintenance to this commit. Independently consider filtering backend iterations with implementation::supported_by_runtime_system() if the fuzzers must run safely across hosts with unsupported compiled implementations."}
